+    /**
+     * Whether a page's TOP gap is written as a 1x1 table row instead of as {@code w:before}.
+     *
+     * <p>Google Docs DROPS {@code w:spacing w:before} on the first paragraph of a page: a
+     * controlled probe asked 55.15 pt and Google rendered 0.33 pt, while a 1x1
+     * {@code w:trHeight w:hRule="exact"} row in the same position bought 55.83 pt. That is the
+     * uniform, constant-in-points upward shift every page of a zero-margin document shows in
+     * Google and not in LibreOffice (FINDINGS/18_displacement-page-top-before-DROPPED-105000-f1x.md,
+     * probe TOPA vs TOPD).
+     *
+     * <p>The row is FLOW-NEUTRAL: {@code beforeTw} keeps its value for {@code fitPage},
+     * {@code resync} and the shave arithmetic, so the page's measured height and every page break
+     * are exactly what they were - {@code spacingTw} sums {@code w:trHeight} at any depth. Only
+     * the rendered construct changes. Gated by {@code -Dp2w.topgaprow=1} until it is measured
+     * through Google.
+     */
+    private static final boolean TOPGAP_ROW =
+            "1".equals(System.getProperty("p2w.topgaprow"));
